## Tool-source excerpts used as specifications (`docs/tool-src/`)
These are verbatim excerpts, extracted via `inspect.getsource` / `deparse` from the versions
shipped in the nf-core/rnaseq 3.26 containers, kept so that byte-identity claims can be
audited against the exact code that produced the goldens. They are not compiled into anything.
- `rseqc-5.x-relevant.py`, `rseqc-inner_distance.py` — RSeQC (Liguo Wang et al.), GPL-3.0.
- `dupradar-1.38-relevant.R` — dupRadar (Sergi Sayols et al.), GPL-3.0.

If redistributing the GPL excerpts is a concern for your use, delete `docs/tool-src/`;
nothing depends on it at build or test time. The behaviours they document are also
described in prose in `crates/umbam/COMPAT.md`.

## Rust dependencies
See `Cargo.lock`; all crates are MIT/Apache-2.0 dual-licensed or MIT (noodles, rayon,
zlib-rs/flate2, clap, anyhow, crc32fast).

## CUDA
`crates/umgpu` links against CUDA 13, CCCL/CUB, and optionally nvCOMP 5 (feature `nvcomp`).
These are not redistributed; see NVIDIA's license terms.

## Data
No sequencing data is in this repository. `data-manifest.json` lists the public Geuvadis
samples (ENA) and GENCODE annotation used, with checksums.
